From bff79e5a82b7cd87090ecd553470b24b7aa99b40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hisxo <16657045+hisxo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:51:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dsv41: coupled drafts (TF_DS_COUPLED_DRAFTS): at T > 0 the
 drafter draws with the target's keyed noise

The DSpark Markov loop takes each step's argmax. At temperature > 0 the target draws its token
by Gumbel-max over its top-k, with noise keyed by (seed, position, token id) (sampling.zig), so
a draft lands only when the target's draw falls on the drafter's argmax. With
TF_DS_COUPLED_DRAFTS=<lambda>, each step draws instead the way the target will draw that
position: sampleRow's rule (top_k, top_p, min_p) on the drafter's scores, with the target's
own keyed noise scaled by lambda (1: the target's very draw on the drafter's scores; 0: the
argmax). Where the drafter and the target agree on the winner of the same noise, the draft
lands. The target's tokens never change: the verification keeps the target's own draw.

The kernel pair (coupled_draft.cu, embedded as the dsv41_coupled fatbin): each rank's 32 best
columns of a step's scores (a sorted list per warp, merged pairwise), their gather over the
ranks, then one warp merges them and draws. The coupled loop runs only in passes where a stream
samples (pass graphs keyed by it); a top_k of 0 drafts over the 32 best. Thinking at T=1
(code, prose, structured, security Q&A; 768 tokens each): 73.1 -> 75.3 tok/s at lambda 0.5,
1,053 -> 1,015 rounds, same tokens; the drafter pass costs 0.25 ms more.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012LKX4U7yxGzgs3Ejvas9Q7
